2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexios III Megas Komnenos''' (Greek: Αλέξιος Μέγας Κομνηνός; 5 October 1338 – 20 March 1390),[1] or '''Alexius III''', was Emperor of Trebizond from December 1349 until his death. He is perhaps the best-documented ruler of tha
2 CONC t country, and his reign is distinguished by a number of religious grants and literary creations. ...
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/TREBIZOND.htm#AlexiosIIITrebizondB<br/>
2 CONT '''KALOIOANNES Angelos Doukas Megas Komnenos''', illegitimate son of BASILEIOS Emperor in Trebizond & his second (bigamous) wife Eirene --- (5 Oct 1338-20 Mar 1390).  The Chronicle of Michael Panaretos records the birth 5 Oct 1338
2 CONC  of "the lord John Komnenos, who later was named Alexios…the second son of the lord Basil"[107].  The Chronicle of Michael Panaretos records that "his sons, the lord Alexios and the lord Kalojannes, were sent…along with their moth
2 CONC er" to Constantinople after the death of "the emperor lord Basil the Grand Komnenos" in 1340[108].  The Chronicle of Michael Panaretos records that "the lord John Komnenos" was sent to Constantinople, dated to Nov 1345 from the co
2 CONC ntext[109].  He succeeded his uncle in 1349 as '''ALEXIOS III Emperor in Trebizond'''.  The Chronicle of Michael Panaretos records that "Basil Komnenos´s second son, the lord John who was called after his grandfather Alexios" took
2 CONC  the throne 22 Dec 1349 "with the empress his mother the Lady Irene the Grand Komnene" and was crowned "in the church of St Eugenios" on 21 Jan [1350][110].  He founded the monastery of Dyonissiou on Mount Athos.  His reign was ma
2 CONC rked by struggles between the emirs who were his sons-in-law, and with the Genoese authorities of Crimea who wanted to extend their commercial privileges[111].  The Chronicle of Michael Panaretos records that in 1361 "the people w
2 CONC ere nearly revolting against the emperor" and that 27 Oct 1363 "some of the nobles, the Kabazitai, the grand logothetes Lord George Scholaris and others fell upon" the emperor while he "was sitting by the St Gregory river near Kat
2 CONC abaton" and "pursued him until the citadel"[112].  The Chronicle of Michael Panaretos records that "Glitzuasthlanes" besieged "places of ours in Chaldia" in Mar 1367[113].  The Chronicle of Michael Panaretos records the death 20 M
2 CONC ar 1390 of "the emperor lord Alexios the Grand Komnenos, the second son of Lord Basil the Grand Komnenos" after reigning for forty years and three months, aged 51[114]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (Trebizond St Eugenios 21 Sep 1350) THEODORA Komnene Kantakouzene, daughter of NIKEPHOROS Kantakouzenos sébastokrator & his wife --- ([1340]-before Jun 1400).  The Chronicle of Michael Panaretos records that "the lady Komn
2 CONC ene Kantakouzene, the daughter of Nikephoros Kantakouzenos, first cousin to the emperor of the Romans lord John Kanatakouzenos" arrived "from the City by galley" 3 Sep 1350 and was married to the emperor 21 Sep in the monastery of
2 CONC  St Eugenios, her name being confirmed as "the Lady Theodora" in a later passage[115].  She became a nun in Constantinople in 1390 as THEODOSIA. <br/>
2 CONT ..four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mistress''' (1): ---.  The name of Emperor Alexios III's first mistress is not known.  <br/>
2 CONT ..one illegitimate son
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mistress''' (2): EVDOKIA, daughter of ---.  Nun 1390/1400. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%90%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%B9_III_%D0%92%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%9A%D0%BE%D0%BC%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BD Алексей III Великий Комнин]
2 CONT
2 CONT Алексей был сыном трапезундского императора Василия Великого Комнина от Ирины Трапезундской, законность женитьбы на которой была оспорена константинопольским патриархом; при рождении он получил имя Иоанн. После смерти Василия в 13
2 CONC 40 году трон заняла его первая жена Ирина Палеолог, которая выслала Ирину Трапезундскую и всех детей своего покойного мужа в Константинополь. В результате Иоанн вырос при византийском дворе
