1 OCCU Countess of Vendome, Countess consort of Vendôme; Countess consort of Romont;, Countess consort of Vendôme, Countess consort of Vendôme; Countess consort of Romont, Comtesse, "Bonne Dame" Ou "Mère Des Pauvres"
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Marie of Luxembourg-Saint-Pol (c. 1472 — 1 April 1547) was the ruling Countess Regnant of Soissons and Saint-Pol between 25 October 1482 and 1 April 1547. She was additionally made Countess consort of Vendôme th
2 CONC rough her marriage to Francis, Count of Vendôme.[1] After the death of her husband, she became regent of the County of Vendôme as the guardian of her son''', Charles de Bourbon.[2]
2 CONT Life
2 CONT '''Marie was the elder daughter and principal heiress''' of Peter II of Luxembourg, Count of Saint-Pol and Soissons, and Margaret of Savoy, daughter of Louis I, Duke of Savoy.[3] '''She belonged to the French cadet branch of a dyn
2 CONC asty which had reigned as Dukes of Luxembourg, and whose senior line produced several Holy Roman Emperors before eventually becoming extinct in 1437.'''
2 CONT '''Marie was first married as a child to her maternal uncle, Jacques of Savoy, Count of Romont.''' [3] A commander in the army of Charles the Bold, he was deprived of his appanage, the Vaud, by Swiss armies sent by Berne and Fribo
2 CONC urg. '''This happened shortly before Marie's prospects as heiress were greatly diminished following her grandfather, the French constable Louis de Luxembourg, Count of Saint-Pol's, execution for treason in 1475; which entailed the
2 CONC  sequestration of his property. She inherited the County of Soissons and the County of Saint-Pol after the death of her father in 1482.'''
2 CONT '''Marie's status and part of her French inheritance were restored upon her remarriage to Francis de Bourbon, Count of Vendôme, a prince du sang, in 1487.[4] Although she had a younger sister''', Francisca of Luxembourg, who wed P
2 CONC hilip of Cleves, Lord of Ravenstein, and her father had several younger brothers, '''she brought vast revenues and estates to the House of Bourbon. These included the counties of Saint-Pol and Soissons in Picardy, Ligny, and Marle
2 CONC , as well as the Château de Condé which was later passed down as a residence to the Princes of Condé: the descendants of her grandson''', Louis de Bourbon, 1st Prince of Condé.
2 CONT '''When her husband Francis died''' in 1495, '''she became guardian of their minor son and heir''' Charles. '''This entailed management of the lands he inherited from his father as well as her own. During this period, she enlarged
2 CONC  the Collégiale Saint Georges, rebuilt the Church of Saint Martin, and donated the Porte Saint Georges-aux-Bourgeois-de-Vendôme to become the Mairie.'''
2 CONT '''Her great-granddaughter was crowned''' Mary, Queen of Scots in 1542.
2 CONT '''She died in 1547 in the château de Fère-en-Tardenois in Picardy, and was buried with her second husband in Vendôme.'''
2 CONT Issue
2 CONT '''Marie's first marriage was to Jacques of Savoy, Count of Romont. They had:'''
2 CONT *Louise-Françoise of Savoy (d. 1511), died childless after her marriage to Count Henry III of Nassau-Breda.[5]
2 CONT '''Marie's second marriage was to Francis de Bourbon, Count of Vendôme. They had:'''
2 CONT *Charles de Bourbon (1489–1537), Duke of Vendôme.[6]
2 CONT *Francis de Bourbon (1491–1545), Count of Saint Pol and Chaumont, and Duke of Estouteville.[7]
2 CONT *Cardinal Louis de Bourbon (1493–1557), Archbishop of Sens.
2 CONT *Antoinette de Bourbon (1494–1583), married Claude, Duke of Guise[8]
2 CONT *Louise de Bourbon (1495–1575), Abbess of Fontevrault.
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marie_I,_Countess_of_Saint-Pol_and_Soissons
2 CONT ________
2 CONT '''Marie of Luxembourg'''1,2
2 CONT Last Edited	11 Aug 2009
2 CONT F, #18350,''' d. 1 April 1547'''
2 CONT '''Father'''	Peter II de Luxembourg, Comte de Brienne, Roussy, Soissons, Marle, & St. Pol b. c 1440, d. 25 Oct 1482
2 CONT '''Mother'''	Margaret de Savoy b. 1439, d. 9 Mar 1483
2 CONT Charts	
2 CONT 14 Generation Pedigree of George III, King of Great Britain & Ireland
2 CONT 14 Generation Pedigree of Friedrich Wilhelm III, King of Prussia
2 CONT '''     Marie of Luxembourg Countess of St. Pol, Ligny & Enghein, heiress of Marle & Soissons. She married Jacob (Jacques) de Savoy, Count of Romont''', son of Louis I, Duke of Savoy and Anne de Lusignan, Princess of Cyprus, '''in
2 CONC  1460.3,2 A contract for the marriage of Marie of Luxembourg and François de Bourbon, 4th Count & 1st Duke de Vendome was signed on 8 September 1487 at Ham, Flanders, Belgium.2 Marie of Luxembourg died on 1 April 1547 at Chateau d
2 CONC e la Fere, France; Buried at St. Georges, Vendome.'''2
2 CONT '''Family 1'''
2 CONT Jacob (Jacques) de Savoy, Count of Romont b. 12 Nov 1450, d. 30 Jan 1486
2 CONT '''Child	'''
2 CONT *Francoise Louise de Savoy4 d. 17 Sep 1511
2 CONT '''Family 2'''
2 CONT '''François de Bourbon, 4th Count & 1st Duke de Vendome''' b. 1470, d. 2 Oct 1495
2 CONT '''Children	'''
2 CONT *Sir Charles IV de Bourbon, Duke of Vendome, Count of Soissons, Marle, Conversano+ b. 2 Jun 1489, d. 25 Mar 1537
2 CONT *Francois I de Bourbon, Duke d'Estouteville, Comte de St. Pol & Chaumont+5 b. 6 Oct 1491, d. 1 Sep 1545
2 CONT *Antoinette de Bourbon+ b. 25 Dec 1493, d. 22 Jan 1583
