1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Prince (Shahzada) Imam Quli Amanu’llah Mirza ibn ‘Abbas al-Husaini al-Musavi al-Safawi Bahadur Khan. b. at Isfahan, 12th November 1602. Blinded on the orders of his father, 1627. He was k. (executed) at Alamut, Aug
2 CONC ust 1632, having had issue, one son:
2 CONT
2 CONT a) Prince (Shahzada) Najaf Quli Mirza. b. ca. 1625. He was k. at Alamut, 1632.
2 CONT
2 CONT Imam Qoli Mirza, the third and last son, then became the crown prince ( after Mohammad Bagher Mirza and Mohammad Khodabandeh). Abbas groomed him carefully for the throne but, for some reason, in 1627, he had him partially blinded 
2 CONC and imprisoned in Alamut.  It will be Mohammad Bagher Mirza's son, Sam Mirza/Shah Safi, who will succeed Shah Abbas I. 
