2 CONT Biography [ edit | modify the code ] Renée d'Anjou is the daughter and heiress of Nicolas d'Anjou-Mezieres and Gabrielle Villebois-Mareuil. His father is the last descendant of the Dukes of Anjou , the bastard of Charles IV Maine 
2 CONC , Louis, Baron de Mezieres 2 . She was born October 21, 1550 3 . Son of absence, his parents left him the whole land: the Marquis of Mezieres, the riding of Saint-Fargeau and the lordships of Mareuil and Villebois .
2 CONT
2 CONT She married in 1566 François de Bourbon , Duke of Montpensier 4 , Prince Dauphin of Auvergne and future Duke of Montpensier . They only son, Henri de Bourbon , born in 1573 .
2 CONT
2 CONT She lived in the castle of Champigny-sur-Veude that belonged to the family of her husband. You can still visit a Holy Chapel , where a stained glass represents to her husband. A statue there is their son Henry, kneeling with hands
2 CONC  joined; this character is very similar to King Henry IV, by facial features and clothing.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1576, the land of Saint-Fargeau is erected in the Duchy-peerage in favor of the couple. In 1582, her husband inherits the duchy of Montpensier and becomes one of the leading princes of the blood.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sometimes given to the date of his death 1597 years but it seems that she died "in the prime of life" 5 , before 1586 6 .
