2 CONC , at the insistence of his cousin, allows marriage to the delight of it in however advising him to marry quickly before the news will know. When the courtiers heard of this project, they protested in effect: Lauzun comes from an i
2 CONC mpoverished family and who has no importance to the court; there is between him and the Grande Mademoiselle a huge social gap. Three days after authorizing marriage, Louis XIVsummoned his cousin to withdraw the right to marry Lauz
