2 CONC  Bethencourts from Béthencourt, Sigy-en-Bray - an escutcheon with an oblique band and, on the right of this, an eagle.33  Regnault habitually resided in Saint-Maurice, near Gaillefontaine, and was the constable of the forest of Be
2 CONC auvoir-sur-Lyons (now Beauvoir-en-Lyons, Argueil, Dieppe, Seine-Maritime, France).33,34 In 1428 Regnault (IV) ceded the lands of Béthencourt to Regnault (V) who was creditor of Jean (IV).33 Regnault (V) passed the fief of Béthenco
2 CONC urt to his son Collard.33
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Regnault de Bethencourt (V) include:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * +  12  i.   Collard de Bethencourt was born circa 1400 at Caux, France. He married Tiphaïne Hurpé at France. 
