1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/False_Dmitry_III False Dmitry III] (Russian: Лжедмитрий III, tr. Lzhedmitrii III; died July 1612), historically known as Pseudo-Demetrius III, was the last and most enigmatic of three
2 CONC  pretenders to the Russian throne who claimed to be the youngest son of Ivan the Terrible; Tsarevich Dmitry. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT He appeared suddenly from Estonia, across the Narva River, to the Ingermanland town of Iivananlinna (Ivangorod), proclaiming himself Tsarevich Dmitry Ivanovich on March 28, 1611. The Cossacks, ravaging the environs of Moscow, ackn
2 CONC owledged him as Tsar on March 2, 1612, and under threat of vengeance in case of non-compliance, the gentry of Pskov also "kissed the cross" (i.e., swore allegiance) to the rebel/criminal of Pskov (псковский вор), as he was usually
2 CONC  nicknamed. On May 18, 1612 he fled from Pskov, was seized and delivered up to the authorities at Moscow, and was secretly executed there.
