2 CONC orraine. Louis, Duke of Orléans, born 3 February 1549, died 24 October 1549. Charles IX, King of France, born 27 June 1550. Henry III, King of France, born 19 September 1551, also briefly King of Poland. Margaret of France, born 1
2 CONC 4 May 1553, married Henry IV, King of France. Hercules, Duke of Anjou, born 18 March 1555, later known as Francis, Duke of Alençon and Anjou. Victoria of France, born 24 June 1556, died 17 August 1556. Joan of France, stillborn. H
2 CONC enry II also had three illegitimate children:
2 CONT
2 CONT By Filippa Duci:[22] Diane, duchesse d'Angoulême (1538–1619). At the age of fourteen, the younger Diane married Orazio Farnese, Duke of Castro,[23] who died in battle in 1553. Her second marriage was to François, Duke of Montmoren
2 CONC cy.[24] By Lady Janet Stewart (1508–1563), the illegitimate daughter of James IV of Scotland:[25] Henri d'Angoulême (1551 – June 1586). He was legitimized and became governor of Provence. By Nicole de Savigny:[26] Henri de Saint-R
2 CONC émy (1557–1621). He was given the title of Count of Saint-Rémy. One of his last descendants was Jeanne de Valois-Saint-Rémy, Countess de la Motte, famous for her role in the Affair of the Diamond Necklace at the court of Louis XVI
2 CONC . Prophecy[edit] Royal styles of King Henry II France moderne.svg Reference style	His Most Christian Majesty Spoken style	Your Most Christian Majesty Alternative style	Monsieur le Roi Nostradamus (1503–1566), a French apothecary a
2 CONC nd astrological writer known for his prophecies, is said by most commentators to have become famous when one of his quatrains was construed as a prediction of the death of King Henry II:
2 CONT
2 CONT CI, Q 35 The young lion shall overcome the older one, on the field of combat in single battle, He shall pierce his eyes in a golden cage, Two forces one, then he shall die a cruel death.
2 CONT
2 CONT But, in fact, the link was first proposed in print only in 1614,[27] fifty-five years after the event and forty-eight after Nostradamus' death; thus it qualifies as a postdiction, or vaticinium ex eventu. The Italian astrologer Lu
2 CONC ca Gaurico, a contemporary of Nostradamus, is also said[by whom?] to have predicted the king's death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Portrayals[edit] Henri or Henry has had three notable portrayals on the screen. He was played by a young Roger Moore in the 1956 film Diane, opposite Lana Turner in the title role and Marisa Pavan as Catherine de Medici. In the 19
2 CONC 98 film Ever After, he was portrayed by Dougray Scott. In the 2013 CW series Reign he is played by Alan Van Sprang.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nostradamus predicts with remarkable accuracy the death of the "Deformed" King, inevitably dyeing because of his ill-fated eye wound 11 days after the jousting with spears.
