1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Louis de Valois, prince de France est né le 3 février 1549 à Fontainebleau et mort le 24 octobre 1550. Deuxième fils du roi de France Henri II et de Catherine de Médicis, il reçoit en apanage dès sa naissance le du
2 CONC ché d'Orléans et prend le nom de Louis III d'Orléans. Son éducation et sa garde furent confiées à Diane de Poitiers. Ses parents avaient des projets pour leur quatrième enfant. Ils lui réservaient le titre de duc d'Urbino, qui app
2 CONC artenait à la famille Médicis, celle de sa mère. Néanmoins, sa mort prématurée éloigna cette tentative des projets de la famille royale.
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/116916572/louis-de_france
2 CONT * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_of_Valois en.wikipedia.org...] ; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis de France (3 February 1549 – 24 October 1550), also known as Louis III, Duke of Orléans was the second son and fourth child of Henry II (31 March 1519 – 10 July 1559), King of France and his wife, Catherine de' Medici, daugh
2 CONC ter of Lorenzo II de' Medici, Duke of Urbino and his wife Madeleine de La Tour d'Auvergne. He died aged eight months.
2 CONT
2 CONT Life
2 CONT
2 CONT After their marriage, Henry and Catherine waited several years before having children. Various remedies were not effective until they, at least according to the voices of the court, turned to the court physician Fernel. In a matte
2 CONC r of twelve years (since the birth of the Dauphin Francis in 1544 to the birth of Victoria and Joan in 1556), Catherine gave birth to ten children. Louis was born on 3 February 1549 at the Palace of Fontainebleau, as the second so
2 CONC n and fourth child of Henry II of France and his Queen Consort, Catherine de' Medici, a member of the House of Medici. He was second in line to the throne, as his older sisters could not inherit under Salic law. Since birth, he wa
2 CONC s entrusted with the duchy of Orléans. Just like his older brother, he was given into the care of Diane de Poitiers, his father's possible mistress and reportedly shared the same nursery with his brother and sister, Francis and El
2 CONC isabeth and later, his brother Charles. He was present when Mary, Queen of Scots arrived at Henry's court. She had come to marry Francis, the future King of France and King consort of Scots. There are reports that his parents had 
2 CONC plans for Louis. They wanted him to become the future Duke of Urbino, a title which belonged exclusively to the Medici family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT
2 CONT Freer's account states that Louis died in 1549, not 1550:
2 CONT
2 CONT After receiving a splendid christening in October 1549, said to be of "extraordinary splendour"[1] in Saint-Germain-en-Laye,[1] a christening of fatal consequences to the infant prince,[1] Louis died at Mantes-la-Jolie, after the 
2 CONC solemnity from the effects of a chill taken while being handed from one state functionary to another.[1] Catherine de' Medici submitted the more readily to the absence of her infant son.[1] The Parisians demonstrated their loyalty
2 CONC  through a series of acts: the municipality gave a piece of bread to every poor person in Paris[1] and the citizens regaled by a display of fireworks on a grand scale in the Place facing the Hôtel de Ville[1].
2 CONT
2 CONT Other accounts
2 CONT
2 CONT Other accounts dismiss Freer's. The genealogy sites Roglo.eu[2] and Genealogy(.euweb.cz)[3] state that Louis died in 1550, Roglo even giving a date for his baptism, 19 May 1549[2] and gives his godparents as John III of Portugal, 
2 CONC Mary of Guise and Ercole II d'Este, Duke of Ferrara[2].
2 CONT
2 CONT Legacy
2 CONT
2 CONT Had he lived, he would have ascended the throne in 1560, when his older brother died. Instead, his younger brother Charles became king, but he had just one daughter (who died aged six and it would have been impossible for her to s
2 CONC ucceed anyway, because she had been a girl), Marie-Elisabeth. His youngest brother Alexandre-Édouard became king, but he had no heirs and the House of Valois ceased to exist. Henry, King of Navarre became king (the first king from
2 CONC  the House of Bourbon).
