1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Children of Regnault de Bethencourt (IV) and Felipa de Troyes were as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT >* +  23  i.   Maciot de Bethencourt was born illegitimate circa 1390 at France.  Maciot de Bethencourt married Lerianda de Gardaleme at France. He died between 1454 and 1458 at Madeira.
2 CONT >* +  24  ii.   Henri de Bettencourt was born illegitimate circa 1390 at France. He married Marguérite de Béthencourt, daughter of Maciot de Bethencourt and Lerianda de Gardaleme, at Islas Canarias. He married Lerianda de Gardalem
2 CONC e at France.
2 CONT
2 CONT >* +  25  iii.   Georges de Bethencourt was born circa 1390 at France. He married Elvira Gonçalvez de Avilla, daughter of Estevan Dominguez de Ávila and Ximena Blasquez, at Valladolid, Castile.
2 CONT
2 CONT >* +  26  iv.   '''Inês de Bethencourt''' (I) was born circa 1390 at Grainville-la-Teinturière, Cany-Barville, Dieppe, Seine-Maritime, France. She married Guillien de Las Casas (I), son of Alfonso de Las Casas (I), at France. Ther
2 CONC e is a question as to which de las Casas brother Inês was married to. Some sources (Guía histórica del Museo Militar Regional de Canarias por Juan Tous Melié) give Inês' husband as Juan de las Casas, who was Guillien's brother. On
2 CONC  the other hand, Guillien is presented by some genealogists as the husband of Leonor González de Guzmán.
2 CONT
2 CONT >* +  27  v.   Jean de Bethencourt (V) was born in 1432 at Caux, France. He married Jeanne de Bethencourt (III), daughter of Collard de Bethencourt and Tiphaíne Hurpé, circa 1469 at France. He married Jeanne de Noyon, daughter of 
2 CONC Crespin de Noyon, in 1475 at France. He died on 21 Mar 1506. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''in: Béthencourts 1200-2000 <http://web.meganet.net/bettenco/bett0007.htm#t7>''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===================================
2 CONT 26. Inês de Bethencourt (I) (Regnault, Jean, Jean, Jean, Regnault, Philippe, Jean) (suffix added for clarification)259,33,9,235,33,9,235 was also known as Inês de Braquemont after her grandmother.260 She was perhaps illegitimate.3
2 CONC 3 She was also known as Agnès de Bettencourt.235 She was also known as Inês de Bettencourt.9 She was born circa 1390 at Grainville-la-Teinturière, Cany-Barville, Dieppe, Seine-Maritime, France.33 She married '''Guillien de Las Cas
2 CONC as (I), son of Alfonso de Las Casas (I), at France.''' There is a question as to which de las Casas brother Inês was married to. Some sources (Guía histórica del Museo Militar Regional de Canarias por Juan Tous Meliá) '''give Inês
2 CONC ' husband as Juan de las Casas, who was Guillien's brother. On the other hand, Guillien is presented by some genealogists as the husband of Leonor González de Guzmán.261,9'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Guillien de Las Casas (I) (suffix added for clarification)261,248 was also known as Guillen de Las Casas.9 He was born circa 1390 at Seville, Spain.72 He was Lord of the unoccupied Canary Islands. He had inherited the right to con
2 CONC quer Gran Canaria and Gomeira from his father. Either in agreement with his brothers or by their deaths and through inheritance, he gained the right to conquer all four islands as yet unoccupied.262 He was "alcaide" or Commander o
2 CONC f the militia of Seville.263 On 25 Mar 1430 he purchased from the Conde de Niebla the lordship of the occupied islands, Fuerteventura and Ferro, leaving only Lanzarote.264
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Inês de Bethencourt (I) and Guillien de Las Casas (I) both born at Spain were as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT +  43  i.   Inês de Las Casas (II) was born circa 1410. She married Fernán Peraza (I), son of Gonzalo Perez Martel. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     44  ii.   Alfonso de Las Casas (II) (suffix added for clarification)265,266,266 was born after 1420.267 
2 CONT
