1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * from [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ismihan_Sultan '''Wikipedia'''], the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ismihan Sultan''' (c. 1544 – 7 August 1585) was an Ottoman princess, the daughter of Selim II (reign 1566-74) and Nurbanu Sultan. She was the granddaughter of Suleiman the Magnificent (reign 1520-66) and his favourite consort a
2 CONC nd legal wife Hürrem Sultan, sister of Sultan Murad III (reign 1574-95) and aunt of Sultan Mehmed III (reign 1595-1603).
2 CONT
2 CONT =Biography=
2 CONT
2 CONT In contrast, strong alliances were made for the daughters of Selim, the prince who would succeed Suleiman: Emahan married Sokollu Mehmed, Gevherhan the admiral Piyalen, and Şah the chief falconer Hasan Agha. On 1 August 1562 Sulei
2 CONC man celebrated the triple wedding of his heir Selim's daughters Esmahan, Gevherhan and Şah to Sokollu Mehmed Pasha, Piyale Pasha and Hasan Agha respectively. In September 1566, upon the death of her grandfather Suleiman the Magnif
2 CONC icent, she came to Istanbul with her mother and sisters, and enjoyed great power in Topkapı Palace. She was very influential in the harems of Selim II and of her brother Murad III, and was at the bottom of many palace schemes. Aft
2 CONC er the death of the grand vizier Sokollu Mehmed Pasha, the princess's first choice for a new husband, Ösdemiroğlu Osman Pasha was not interested. Her next choice was Kalaylıkoz Ali Pasha, the governor of Buda, who agreed to the ma
2 CONC rriage, but when the imperial order came demanding his divorce, his wife's sorrow and suffering were said to have caused the city to revolt. Her marriage to Ali Pasha took place in 1584. Ismihan sultan died on 7 August 1585, and w
2 CONC as buried in Hagia Sophia Mosque.
2 CONT
2 CONT =References=
2 CONT
2 CONT * "Turkey: The Imperial House of Osman". web.archive.org. Retrieved 6 February 2014.
