1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Dorothy Paleologus''' (August 1606 – 1681) – Remained in Landulph after Theodore's death. Dorothy married William Arundel, son[48] or grandson[49] of Alexander Arundel, who Nicholas Lower had purchased Clifton H
2 CONC all from.[48] The entries recording the marriage in the marriage registers at Landulph and at William's home parish of St Mellion grandly describe Dorothy as of "imperial stock" (Dorothea Paleologus de stirpe imperatorum).[23][48]
2 CONC  Since the registers at St. Dominic were accidentally destroyed, it is impossible to determine whether Dorothy and William had children,[49] but it is unlikely since Dorothy was fifty years old by the time of the marriage.[23] Dor
2 CONC othy was buried in Landulph in 1681.[50]
2 CONT
2 CONT *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodore_Paleologus#Family_and_children
