2 CONT Henri, Prince of Condé (1588–1646)
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Henri de Bourbon (September 1, 1588 – December 26, 1646) became Prince of Condé shortly after his birth, following the death of his father Henry I in battle. As a member of the reigning House of Bourbon, he was a Prince du Sang.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Charlotte of Montmorency in 1609 and had three children, all of them protagonists of the Fronde:
2 CONT
2 CONT -1. Anne Genevieve of Bourbon-Condé (1619-1679), married to Henry II of Orleans, Duke of Longueville
2 CONT
2 CONT -2. Louis II of Bourbon the Great Condé (1621-1686)
2 CONT
2 CONT -3. Armand of Bourbon, Prince of Conti (1629-1666)
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrás / Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_II_de_Bourbon,_prince_de_Condé
