2 CONT
2 CONT Louis de Bourbon, Prince of Condé (8 September 1621 – 11 December 1686) was a French general and the most famous representative of the Condé branch of the House of Bourbon. Prior to his father's death in 1646, he was styled the Du
2 CONC c d'Enghien. For his military prowess he was renowned as le Grand Condé.
2 CONT
