1 OCCU Illegitimate son of King of France Henri IV and Gabrielle d'Estree made legitimate in 1595 and assigned Duchy of Beaufort
1 TITL Duc of Vendome and of Etampes
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/C%C3%A9sar_of_Bourbon,_Duke_of_Vend%C3%B4me
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00003655&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT César de Bourbon, Duc de Vendôme (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #114501, b. 3 June 1594, d. 22 October 1665
2 CONT
2 CONT César de Bourbon, Duc de Vendôme was born illegitimately on 3 June 1594 at Château de Coucy, Picardie, France. (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Henri IV, Roi de France and Gabrielle d'Estrées, Duchesse de Beaufort. (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Françoise de Lorraine-Mercouer, daughter of Philip Emanuel de Lorraine, Duc de Lorraine-Mercouer and Marie de Luxembourg-Penthièvre, on 7 July 1609. (1) He died on 22 October 1665 at age 71 at Paris, France.1
2 CONT
2 CONT In January 1595 his birth was legitimised. (1) 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was created Duc de Vendôme in 1598. (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of César de Bourbon, Duc de Vendôme and Françoise de Lorraine-Mercouer
2 CONT
2 CONT -1. Louis de Vendôme, Duc de Vendôme et de Mercoeur+ b. Dec 1612, d. 6 Aug 1669 (1) 
2 CONT
2 CONT -2. Elizabeth de Vendôme+ b. Aug 1614, d. 19 May 1664 (3) 
2 CONT
2 CONT -3. François de Vendôme, Duc de Beaufort b. 5 Jan 1616, d. 25 Jun 1669 (1)
2 CONT
