2 TITL James VI, of Scotland
2 NOTE James VI and I was born 19 June 1566 – 27 March 1625 and was King of Scotland as James VI, and King of England and King of Ireland as James I. He ruled in Scotland as James VI from 24 July 1567, when he was only one year old, succ
3 CONC eeding his mother Mary, Queen of Scots. Regents governed during his minority, which ended officially in 1578, though he did not gain full control of his government until 1581. On 24 March 1603, as James I, he succeeded the last Tu
3 CONC dor monarch of England and Ireland. 
3 CONT He then ruled England, Scotland and Ireland for 22 years, often using the title King of Great Britain, until his death at the age of 58.
3 CONT
3 CONT Read more about James VI in his profile.
