0 @N6000000006444108124@ NOTE Antoine de Bourbon
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
1 CONT Antoine de Bourbon, duc de Vendôme (22 April 1518 – 17 November 1562).
1 CONT
1 CONT He was born at La Fère, Picardie, France, the son of Charles IV de Bourbon, duc de Vendôme (1489-1537) and his wife, formerly Francoise d'Alencon (-1550). He was the older brother of Louis I de Bourbon, Prince de Condé.
1 CONT
1 CONT On 20 October 1548 at Moulins he married Jeanne d'Albret, Queen of Navarre, daughter of Henri d'Albret (Henri II of Navarre) and his wife Margaret of Angoulême.
1 CONT
1 CONT He died at Les Andelys, Eure.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Issue
1 CONT Henri, duc de Beaumont (1551-1553) 
1 CONT Henri IV, King of France (1553-1610) 
1 CONT Madeleine (1556) 
1 CONT Catherine de Bourbon (1559-1604). Married Henry I, Duke of Lorraine in 1599. 
1 CONT Retrieved from "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antoine_de_Bourbon"
0 @N6000000001956325956@ NOTE
1 CONT Changed his name to Epperson to establish an English identity.
0 @N6000000001563054694@ NOTE James V and Mary de Guise
1 CONT He supported France against Henry VIII. Protestant England and Catholic Scotland fought at the battle of Solway Moss in 1542. The news that his army had been defeated destroyed the health of the king. His daughter, Mary, was born 
1 CONC a week before his death. The king said, "It came with a lass (Marjorie Bruce), it will pass with a lass."
1 CONT James was gifted in many ways, but he lacked persistence and calculation to be a great King. When he was on a prosperous course, he did well, but when things turned against him, he did not hold up. His death presented Henry VIII w
1 CONC ith an opportunity which he had long sought. The baby girl who was now the ruler of Scotland had for her nearest male kinsman the King of England (her great-uncle). He had a son of marriageable age and the little Queen was betroth
1 CONC ed to the Prince of Wales. History had repeated itself. On the death of Alexander III, the nearest male kinsman of the Maid of Norway had been Edward I, Longshanks, who had a marriageable son and who knew how to exploit such a sit
1 CONC uation. 
1 CONT Henry overplayed his hand acting as if he were already king of Scotland. The Scottish reaction was prompt. The Scottish Parliament denounced a treaty with England (the Greenwich Treaties). Henry then loosed his troops upon Scotlan
1 CONC d with instructions to kill, burn and spoil. English aggression thus drove Scotland to ally with France once again.
0 @N6000000001579447695@ NOTE James V and Mary de Guise
1 CONT He supported France against Henry VIII. Protestant England and Catholic Scotland fought at the battle of Solway Moss in 1542. The news that his army had been defeated destroyed the health of the king. His daughter, Mary, was born 
1 CONC a week before his death. The king said, "It came with a lass (Marjorie Bruce), it will pass with a lass."
1 CONT James was gifted in many ways, but he lacked persistence and calculation to be a great King. When he was on a prosperous course, he did well, but when things turned against him, he did not hold up. His death presented Henry VIII w
1 CONC ith an opportunity which he had long sought. The baby girl who was now the ruler of Scotland had for her nearest male kinsman the King of England (her great-uncle). He had a son of marriageable age and the little Queen was betroth
1 CONC ed to the Prince of Wales. History had repeated itself. On the death of Alexander III, the nearest male kinsman of the Maid of Norway had been Edward I, Longshanks, who had a marriageable son and who knew how to exploit such a sit
1 CONC uation.
1 CONT Henry overplayed his hand acting as if he were already king of Scotland. The Scottish reaction was prompt. The Scottish Parliament denounced a treaty with England (the Greenwich Treaties). Henry then loosed his troops upon Scotlan
1 CONC d with instructions to kill, burn and spoil. English aggression thus drove Scotland to ally with France once again.
