0 @N6000000005024488905@ NOTE Illigetimate
1 CONT Catholic
1 CONT He was also known as Micer Maciote Betancur.416 He was also known as Massiote de Bethencourt.417 He was also known as Masiote de Bethencourt.418 He was also known as Maciot de Bethancourt.419 He was also known as Maciot de Bettenc
1 CONC ourt.420 He was also known as Mathieu de Bethencourt.421 Maciot is a problem in many ways. There are different views on how he is related to the Bettencourts of France. There is a theory that Maciot was not the son of Regnault but
1 CONC  of Regnault's sister of unknown name. Another theory states that he is the son of Jean (III)'s sister of unknown name. Current opinion favors Regnault as his parent.
1 CONT
1 CONT As to Maciot's wife and children, there are even more problems. Lerianda de Gardaleme is possibly confused with the wife of Maciot's grandson, Maciot (II). Her name is very similar - Leissa Guanartème, her name after converting to
1 CONC  Catholicism.422 He was a Knight of the Order of Malta.423,424 He was a knight of the Order of Rhodes.425 On 9 May 1405 Maciot traveled to the Canary Islands with his Uncle Jean.426,427 He was ruler of the Canary Islands after his
1 CONC  uncle left the islands between Dec 1405 and 1447.428,429,430,431 Maciot attempted, with the assistance of some Castilians, to subdue the island of Gomeira, the Canary Islands, but without success.432 In 1414 the exactions and tyr
1 CONC anny of Maciot de Bethencourt had caused Queen Catherine of Castile to send out three war caravels under the command of Pedro Barba de Campos, Lord of Castro Forte, to control him. Maciot, although only regent, since Jean de Bethe
1 CONC ncourt was still alive, ceded the islands to Barba and then sailed to Madeira, where he sold to Prince Henry of Portugal, surnamed the Navigator, these very islands which he had just ceded to another, together with those which sti
1 CONC ll remained to be conquered. (According to Os Bettencourt, this sale by Maciot to Campos is pure legend) Maciot subsequently granted them again to the Spanish Count de Niebla on 15 Nov 1419 (1418 according to Os Bettencourt). Pedr
1 CONC o Barba de Campos sold them to Fernando Perez of Seville, and the latter again to the aforesaid Count de Niebla, who disposed of them to Guillem de Las Casas, and the latter to his son-in-law Fernan Peraza. Meanwhile, the legitima
1 CONC te proprietor, Jean de Bethencourt, left them by will to his brother Reynaud. It was not until 1479, with the treaty signed at Alcaçova between Affonso V of Portugal and Ferdinand and Isabella of Castile, that the disputes of the 
1 CONC two nations on this point were settled - the Canaries belonged to the Castilians.433,434 In 1415 in Lanzarote, Maciot had a relationship with Teguise, a native woman and daughter of King Guardafia.435 With regard to Maciot's relat
1 CONC ionship with Teguise, it seems that they were never married. They had at least two children, Rodrigo and Inês Margarida. Portuguese genealogists affirm that Maria, another of Maciot's daughters, was also a daughter of Teguise; in 
1 CONC fact, Canarian genealogists refer to this Maria as Leonor or Luisa.436 He built the church of Nossa Senhora de Bethencourt.437 He, acting as representative of Jean de Bethencourt, granted the lordship of the Canary Islands to D. H
1 CONC enrique de Guzmán, Conde de Niebla on 15 Nov 1418 in Seville.438 In 1447 Maciot was taken prisoner on Lanzarote and imprisoned on the island of Ferro. He later fled with his wife to Portugal.439 He sold the Canaries to Prince Henr
1 CONC y the Navigator for the soap trade and other income from Madeira on 9 May 1448.440,441,442,443 He moved with his two daughters and two of his brother's sons to Madeira (Os Bettencourt states that he went with his wife, his eldest 
1 CONC daughter who was the widow of Henri (II), and her two sons who were also his brother's two sons since his daughter was married to his brother (niece-uncle). It was the descendants of Henri (II) who altered the "th" of Bethencourt 
1 CONC to the "tt" of Bettencourt).444,445,446,447
1 CONT
1 CONT _____________________
1 CONT But really the perpetuation of the Bethencourt last name in the Canary Islands and Madeira, comes through Maciot de Bethencourt , Gentleman of the island of Lanzarote and close relative (nephew) of the Conqueror, Jean de Bethencou
1 CONC rt. Although the custom to put in front the maternal last name, has been one of the reasons that this last name has extended so much in the Archipelago as in America, particularly in the countries of canary emigration. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Maciot II of Bethencourt, neighbor of Lanzarote happened to Gran Canaria in 1478, once the island was conquered, of which he was Regidor. He settled down in the villa of Gáldar, marrying with Gives Luisa de Guanarteme ,second cous
1 CONC in of Gives Catherine Guanarteme, heiress of the Throne of Gáldar.,,
